{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And Elohim completed on the seventh day</b> Some say that the days were created, and with the creation of the seventh day the work was completed. This interpretation is worthless. Others say that the bet means 'before,' as in לא תחסום שור בדישו (Deuteronomy 25:4), אך ביום הראשון תשביתו שאור (Exodus 12:15) — and why this difficulty, and is cessation of work not like saying he did no work? So too they interpret ויכל, and likewise וישבות." "The meaning of 'His work which He did' — on the sixth day, before the Sabbath day." "The meaning of 'and He rested on the seventh day from all His work' — from all the creations that He created."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The two scriptural citations are rendered into English for readability, as Ibn Ezra quotes them to illustrate the bet meaning 'before/at'; his Hebrew preserves the original forms."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:44.384006101Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}